{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>So we came to your brother, to Esau.</b> The messengers said to him: You said to him, ״כֹּה אָמַר עַבְדְּךָ יַעֲקֹב״, thereby acknowledging to him regarding the blessings, saying in effect: you are the master, the great one, and I am your servant. But Esau did not accept this and said: he is no servant but rather my brother. This is what they said, ״בָּאנוּ אֶל אָחִיךָ״ — and this is according to the words of Esau himself, who said ״אָחִי הוּא״ and not ״עַבְדִּי״. For by this he revealed to us that his heart is not whole with you; and not only is he not whole with you, but he is also coming toward you — and this can only be to do battle with you. And proof of this: four hundred men are with him, and this can only be for war. Another matter: ״בָּאנוּ אֶל אָחִיךָ״ — as a show of brotherhood and love. However, this too we see contradicted by its opposite, for he is coming out toward you; therefore we are bewildered by the matter. And for this reason Jacob said ״הַצִּילֵנִי נָא מִיַּד אָחִי מִיַּד עֵשָׂו״ (Genesis 32:12) — for he shows himself as a brother, but in truth he is Esau in his wickedness and the cunning deceiver. And ״ה׳ לִי בְּעֹזְרָי״ (Psalms 118:7) — from those who show themselves as helpers and lovers, while hatred is buried in their hearts."], :book :genesis, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:31:28.118888784Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}